Remove non-functional Sec-WebSocket-* headers from DEXSCREENER_WSS_HEADERS

The Sec-WebSocket-Version and Sec-WebSocket-Extensions headers in the dictionary (config.py, lines 30–31) are silently ignored by the websockets library version 12.x. Sec-WebSocket-Version is generated automatically and Sec-WebSocket-Extensions must be negotiated with the extensions argument. These will never reach the server via extra_headers, making them dead code.

The other headers (User-Agent, Accept, Accept-Language, Accept-Encoding, Origin, Referer, Cache-Control, Pragma) are functional and appropriate for bot-detection evasion. Remove the two Sec-* entries to avoid confusion and keep the config accurate.

