Multiple critical issues block this PR: backoff clamping prevents 403 rate-limit handling, and missing Scanner export breaks tests

Backoff logic never reaches 60s due to global clamp

Your 403 handler sets backoff = min(backoff * 3, 60), but lines 243–245 clamp all backoff to 30s:

wait_time = min(backoff, 30)
backoff = min(backoff * 2, 30)
This prevents the intended 10–60s rate-limit backoff. Introduce a max_backoff variable that tracks the ceiling per scenario:

backoff = 1
+max_backoff = 30  # Standard-Maximum für Backoff
consecutive_502_errors = 0
On 403 rotation, set max_backoff = 60; on 502 rotation, reset to 30. Then use:

-wait_time = min(backoff, 30)
+wait_time = min(backoff, max_backoff)
-backoff = min(backoff * 2, 30)
+backoff = min(backoff * 2, max_backoff)
Scanner export missing—tests fail

tests/test_scanner_integration.py imports from scanner import Scanner (lines 15, 28, 40) but scanner.py exports only HighPerformanceScanner (class) and scanner (instance). Add at the end of scanner.py:

